  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant force\nthe next several days. Most areas will have highs in the 90s. The\nGlendive area will have highs near 100 today and will issue an\nExtreme Heat Warning there today from 10 am through 10 pm. \n\nSatellite showcases a large smoke plume stretched from eastern \nOregon across northern Montana. Visibility was 3 to 5SM this \nafternoon and evening but have risen back to P6SM in most areas as\nof 06z. Smoke will continue to be over the area today and tonight\nwith unhealthy air quality and variable visibilities. \n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing for \nseveral days through the weekend with highs in the 90s to around \n100 degrees each day. Conditions will also be dry most of the time with\noccasional shortwave to trigger showers and thunderstorms.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather continuing all week. Low\nconfidence in timing any showers and thunderstorms.\n\nNBM Deviations include HRRR/RAP blends to enhance visibility \nreductions due to smoke.",
